# Monorepo Architecture & Boundaries

Reference full specs in `.cursor/plans/company-brain-saas-plan.md` and `.cursor/plans/repo-structure.md`.

## Layout & Tooling

- Polyglot monorepo: **`uv` workspace** for Python (`apps/api`, `apps/workers`, `packages/*`, `evals`) and **`pnpm`** for Next.js (`apps/web`).
- Expose standard dev/CI entrypoints in root `justfile` (`up`, `migrate`, `dev`, `eval`, `codegen`).

## Strict Acyclic Dependency Graph

Enforce one-way imports across packages:

```text
apps/{api,workers} -> packages/agent -> packages/{brain,connectors,sandbox,surfaces} -> packages/core
```

- `packages/` MUST NEVER import from `apps/`.
- `packages/core` MUST NEVER import from any other workspace package.
- Place Slack/WhatsApp clients and Block Kit renderers in `packages/surfaces` so both `apps/api` and `apps/workers` share them cleanly.

## Service & Contract Boundaries

- **Webhooks (`apps/api/src/ceo_api/webhooks/`)**: Verify signatures, acknowledge fast, debounce via Redis if needed, and dispatch durable work to Temporal — never run LLM calls or sync loops inside HTTP handlers.
- **Temporal Queues (`apps/workers`)**: Keep interactive `agent-queue`, bulk `sync-queue`, and scheduled `jobs-queue` isolated so backfills never block live Slack replies.
- **LangChain Boundary (`packages/agent`)**: Keep all LangChain orchestration (LCEL runnables, ZDR `BaseChatModel` factories, ACL-scoped `BaseRetriever`, `StructuredTool` adapters, `ChatPromptTemplate`s, and `AsyncCallbackHandler` metering) inside `packages/agent` and invoke it only from Temporal `activities/` — preserving both the acyclic dependency graph and deterministic workflows.
- **API Types**: Treat FastAPI OpenAPI output as the single source of truth; generate TypeScript types into `apps/web/src/lib/api-client/` rather than hand-maintaining duplicate DTOs.

## Phased Build Discipline

Only scaffold and populate modules needed for the active phase (Phase 1: core brain + RLS + Slack + Drive/Notion + ACL evals; Phase 2: living memory + approvals + managed connectors; Phase 3: standing jobs + sandbox + Stripe metering; Phase 4: WhatsApp + entity graph + Linear/HubSpot + Terraform).
